<title>ITALY: Olivetti opens higher after analysts' meeting.</title>
<headline>Olivetti opens higher after analysts' meeting.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian information technology group Olivetti opened 8.17 percent higher at 560 lire on the Milan bourse after the company announced plans to raise up to 1.2 trillion lire through asset sales.</p>
<p>Oivetti CEO Roberto Colaninno told financial analysts in Milan on Thursday that Olivetti planned to sell its ailing personal computers business and three other companies by the end of the year, raising 800 billion lire.</p>
<p>A further 400 billion lire would be raised by more asset sales in 1997, Colaninno said.</p>
<p>Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
